  "source_review": [
    "World.emit records time and persistent counters; drain_events clears the queue.",
    "HomeService._publish drains before events_ready; four event kinds schedule a save after the 800 ms debounce. Other timer mutations are dirty for the 30-second periodic save.",
    "HomeService.run schedules save for all admitted commands; timer advancement marks state dirty for periodic save.",
    "PetHomePage._on_events forwards the same batch to HomeView and InboxPanel; service world supplies resident/recipe labels.",
    "HomeView only uses settled events with an extant station for completion badges.",
    "Inbox ignores ordinary activity/meal/nap chatter; refuses are presented by resident status rather than the Inbox."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "One sequential self-review of event routing, not independent or whole-repository review.",
    "AST inventory covers literal emit names in the domain package; classification probes use synthetic events and do not prove every producer is reachable.",
    "No UI rendering or timer scheduling claim from these probes."
  ],
  "observation": [
    "Inbox module docstring claims individually switchable categories, but wanted() currently accepts all four and no category controls were found. Public README describes grouping, not switches. This is a stale internal description, not evidence of a missing promised user control."
  ],
